==================================================
OBJECTIVE
==================================================

The existing Pod Metrics job is primarily used by the testing team to monitor live CPU and memory utilization while performing testing activities.

We now want to make it useful for developers as well.

Developers often need to answer:

"Is this application currently consuming unusually high CPU or memory?"

They generally do NOT need a continuously running monitoring session.

Therefore, introduce two explicit monitoring modes:

1. Snapshot
2. Live Monitoring

The user should choose the mode through a two-option segmented toggle:

[ Snapshot ] [ Live Monitoring ]

Do NOT use a dropdown for this. There are only two mutually exclusive modes.

Snapshot should be the default mode.

Opening the Pod Metrics page must NOT automatically trigger any metrics collection.

==================================================
IMPORTANT EXISTING BEHAVIOR
==================================================

The interactive Pod Metrics flow is:

Application
→ select supported Namespace
→ select polling frequency
→ collect metrics

The interactive Pod Metrics job monitors ONLY the namespace selected by the user.

It must NOT suddenly start collecting all namespaces.

The recently added Insight Engine uses some of the same backend metrics logic but intentionally collects data across multiple/all namespaces for insight generation and restart-related analysis.

DO NOT change, break, or restrict the Insight Engine's existing all-namespace behavior.

Reuse the existing metrics collection logic wherever possible.

==================================================
1. SNAPSHOT MODE
==================================================

Snapshot is a one-time collection.

Flow:

Application
→ Namespace
→ Snapshot selected
→ user clicks "Run Metrics"
→ collect current metrics once
→ display results
→ collection finishes

Do NOT start a persistent polling loop.

Do NOT create a persistent live WebSocket monitoring session for Snapshot.

Do NOT consume one of the active live monitoring session slots after the snapshot completes.

Do NOT automatically execute Snapshot simply because the page is opened.

The user must explicitly click:

Run Metrics

Snapshot represents the current point-in-time state of the selected application + namespace.

==================================================
2. LIVE MONITORING MODE
==================================================

Live Monitoring should retain the existing live metrics behavior.

Flow:

Application
→ Namespace
→ frequency
→ Live Monitoring
→ Start Live Monitoring
→ repeated metrics collection
→ existing WebSocket live updates
→ user manually stops it

Use the existing WebSocket implementation.

Do not create a second live-streaming architecture.

The existing multi-user/session isolation already implemented in the repository must remain intact.

==================================================
3. ROLE-BASED LIVE SESSION TIMEOUT
==================================================

Live Monitoring now needs role-based automatic timeout.

Developer:
- maximum live monitoring duration = 10 minutes
- timeout MUST be enforced by the backend
- do not rely only on a frontend timer

Tester:
- no automatic duration timeout
- can continue until manually stopped

Other authorized roles:
- no automatic duration timeout unless an existing application policy explicitly requires otherwise

The developer UI should clearly show the remaining time.

Example:

Live Monitoring
Running · 07:32 remaining

When the 10-minute limit is reached:

- stop the metrics session cleanly
- terminate associated collection processes
- close the WebSocket appropriately
- release the active session slot
- persist the correct final status
- clearly notify the user why the session stopped

Example:

"Live monitoring stopped: 10-minute developer session limit reached."

Do NOT silently stop the session.

The backend must remain the source of truth for the timeout.

==================================================
4. ACTIVE SESSION LIMIT
==================================================

The existing multi-user work introduced:

MAX_ACTIVE_METRICS_SESSIONS = 10

Keep that behavior.

Snapshot requests must NOT count as active long-running metrics sessions after they complete.

Only active Live Monitoring sessions count toward the limit.

Do not change the limit as part of this task.

Do not allow Snapshot to accidentally consume a live-session slot.

